#: ../../source/quality/hybrid_architecture.md:59
#: 4ae1f9d0643546ffa2787513c9d79377
msgid "3. Architecture & Fallback FAQ"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/hybrid_architecture.md:61
#: 4231543e86e84713970f8e0439c26f53
msgid ""
"3.1. What happens if no prebuilt binary wheel exists for a target "
"platform?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/hybrid_architecture.md:63
#: 1b09eb9f88e94ffabe65319ae3ebdcba
#, python-format
msgid ""
"`findfmt` remains 100% functional on every Python `>=3.11` platform. Once"
" installed from a pure-Python wheel or on an architecture without "
"`findfmt._rust_ext`, `src/findfmt/core.py` catches `ImportError` during "
"initialization and delegates all `find_files()` and `classify_file()` "
"calls to `src/findfmt/_fallback.py` with zero user intervention. Note "
"that runtime fallback applies after installation succeeds: building from "
"source without a matching prebuilt wheel runs the Maturin build hook and "
"requires Cargo by default. In environments without Cargo, set "
"`HATCH_MATURIN_DISABLE=1` before building or installing to produce the "
"pure-Python package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/hybrid_architecture.md:70
#: 0600ad80473b4dd68e2b1a1d6a4c3fb2
msgid "3.2. Why does `findfmt_rs` use PyO3 `abi3-py311`?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/hybrid_architecture.md:72
#: f2bb03658ac04e10a7084982535101f3
msgid ""
"Enabling `abi3-py311` targets CPython's Stable Limited API for Python "
"`3.11` and newer. A single compiled wheel per OS/architecture "
"(`cp311-abi3-*`) installs and runs across Python `3.11`, `3.12`, `3.13`, "
"`3.14`, and `3.15+` without recompiling separate binaries per minor "
"interpreter release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/hybrid_architecture.md:76
#: bcf964cb3f684fcc9910a133b9893b84
msgid "3.3. What happens if native Rust code panics during execution?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/hybrid_architecture.md:78
#: 5afd0ce032b245dd836b43c4659a64ef
msgid ""
"PyO3 converts Rust thread panics across FFI boundaries into "
"`pyo3_runtime.PanicException`, which inherits directly from Python's "
"`BaseException` (alongside `SystemExit` and `KeyboardInterrupt`). Both "
"`classify_file()` and `find_files()` in `src/findfmt/core.py` intercept "
"`pyo3_runtime.PanicException` while allowing all non-panic "
"`BaseException` and `Exception` subclasses to propagate normally. During "
"`find_files()` iteration, already-emitted `(path, relative_path)` "
"occurrences are tracked with a multiplicity counter so fallback replay "
"through `src/findfmt/_fallback.py` neither duplicates delivered records "
"nor drops distinct entries from overlapping search roots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/hybrid_architecture.md:86
#: 1e6fd862f336437caac0a82b899436cc
msgid ""
"3.4. How is MIT license compliance enforced across Rust crate "
"dependencies?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/hybrid_architecture.md:88
#: de3ef37315c94f1b88bc51892c7c8207
msgid ""
"Binary wheels bundle compiled code from `findfmt_rs` and its transitive "
"Cargo dependencies. Every crate in `findfmt_rs/Cargo.lock` is audited by "
"`cargo-deny` (`findfmt_rs/deny.toml`) to permit only OSI-approved "
"permissive licenses (`MIT`, `Apache-2.0`, `BSD-2-Clause`, `BSD-3-Clause`,"
" `Unicode-3.0`, `Zlib`), and full third-party attribution notices are "
"generated into `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md` via `cargo-about` and packaged "
"under `.dist-info/licenses/`."
msgstr ""

